**js/app.js**
```js
document.querySelectorAll('.card').forEach(card => {
  card.tabIndex = 0;
  card.addEventListener('keydown', e => {
    if (e.key === 'Enter') console.log('Open project:', card.querySelector('h2').textContent);
  });
});
console.log('Portfolio ready');
```

Why it works: CSS custom properties keep the dark theme consistent from one place, the auto-fit grid is responsive with zero media queries, and app.js sits at the end of body so the DOM exists before the script runs.

