**js/app.js**
```js
document.getElementById('beta-form').addEventListener('submit', e => {
  e.preventDefault();
  const form = e.target;
  const email = form.email.value.trim();
  const msg = form.querySelector('.msg');
  if (!/^[^@\s]+@[^@\s]+\.[^@\s]+$/.test(email)) {
    msg.textContent = 'Please enter a valid email address.';
    return;
  }
  msg.style.color = '#16a34a';
  msg.textContent = 'Thanks! Check your inbox for the invite.';
  form.reset();
});
```

Why it works: the regex validates format on the client before any request, aria-live announces the result to screen readers, and clamp() scales the hero headline fluidly between breakpoints.

