**js/app.js**
```js
const search = document.getElementById('search');
const posts = [...document.querySelectorAll('.post')];
search.addEventListener('input', () => {
  const q = search.value.toLowerCase();
  posts.forEach(p => {
    const hay = (p.textContent + ' ' + p.dataset.tags).toLowerCase();
    p.hidden = !hay.includes(q);
  });
});
```

Why it works: filtering reads both visible text and data-tags so posts match on hidden metadata, and the hidden attribute removes cards from layout without extra CSS classes.

