**js/app.js**
```js
let count = 0;
document.querySelectorAll('.thumbs button').forEach(btn => {
  btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    document.getElementById('main').src = btn.dataset.src;
  });
});
document.getElementById('add').addEventListener('click', () => {
  const qty = Math.max(1, parseInt(document.getElementById('qty').value, 10) || 1);
  count += qty;
  document.getElementById('count').textContent = count;
});
```

Why it works: thumbnails swap the main image through a data attribute so no image list is duplicated in JS, the qty is clamped to a sane minimum, and the badge is updated from a single counter variable.

